==Polish==
{{wp|lang=pl}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|pl|zlw-opl|książka}}. {{surf|pl|księga|-ka}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{pl-pr|a=pl-książka.ogg;LL-Q809 (pol)-Olaf-książka.wav;LL-Q809 (pol)-Gower-książka.wav|mp=#}}

===Noun===
{{pl-noun|f|dim=książeczka}}

# [[book]] {{gl|collection of sheets of paper bound together to hinge at one edge, containing printed or written material, pictures, etc.}}
# [[book]] {{gl|long work fit for publication, typically prose, such as a novel or textbook, and typically published as such a bound collection of sheets}}
# {{dim of|pl|księga|t=[[ledger]]}} {{gl|book for keeping notes; a record book, a register}}
# {{lb|pl|Middle Polish|in the plural}} [[oxeye daisy]] {{gl|{{taxfmt|Leucanthemum vulgare|species}}}}

====Usage notes====
In Middle Polish, the term was sometimes a diminutive of ''księga'' in the meaning ''book''; however, even by the 16th century, the term gained and has kept a neutral meaning, and is now the standard term for ''book''.

